// A custom event-schema group `meta` (NOT `input`/`output`) carries a
// `region` member. A Read is permitted only if the SAME user formerly
// logged in from region "us-east", matched by a LITERAL on the nested path
// `meta.region`.
//
// The interpreter descends `meta.region` via `field_path` exactly like
// `input.user` — it has no privileged set of group names. A differential
// temporal engine that hardcodes `input`/`output` as the only field groups
// would fail to serialize / read `meta.region`, so the compiled filter
// would see NULL and wrongly deny.
//
// Controls:
//   trace_1: past Login with meta.region "us-east" (matches) -> PERMITTED.
//   trace_2: past Login with meta.region "eu-west" (does not match) -> NOT
//            permitted (the literal genuinely constrains the match).
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user, meta.region: "us-east" }
};
